Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790308799999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the 2850 high is a single-bar spike (bar 117) with a 74.39-point upper tail, and bars 118-120 give no follow-through above it; a failed breakout would rotate price back into the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Upside spike attempts inside this window have repeatedly failed: 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range, so an overshoot above a range top is a recurring pattern here.", "Bar 119 closes at 2684.16, back below the 2771 prior swing high, so the break above that swing high is not yet accepted.", "Near-term momentum has turned down: bars 118 and 119 are the first two consecutive lower closes since bar 113, and bar 119 closes in the lower quarter of its range.", "Bars 87-113 (27 of the last 34 bars before the breakout) traded two-sided inside 2357.18-2680, so an alternative read is a broad trading range with only a marginal upside overshoot, i.e., phase more channel/range than a fresh spike.", "Bars 115 and 116 barely advance (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) between the two strong bars, and the leg from bar 106 to 2850 contains overlapping pullbacks, which is channel rather than pure spike behavior."], "evidence_for": ["The 120-bar window shows an unbroken sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42, 1512.91, 1597.72, 1803.74, 2357.18, 2633.31) and higher swing highs (1944.39, 2771, 2850), which is the core of the bull-trend classification.", "Bar 84 is a large bull trend bar closing at the top of its range with follow-through to 2771 (bars 85-86), showing acceptance above the 1803.74-1974.46 range rather than a one-bar overshoot.", "The compressed final range (bars 73-83 inside 1863.68-1937.76) is a tight-range/bull-flag structure that resolved upward, consistent with trend continuation rather than a top.", "The latest leg (bars 114, 117) closes above both the 2680 range top and the 2771 prior swing high, so the current structure is a breakout to a new high, not a rotation inside the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Bar 120 holds above the 2680 range top and closes above its open (2686.59 versus 2684.16), so no bear breakout or acceptance back inside the range has occurred.", "The bearish bars after the high are small relative to the preceding bull bars (bar 119 range 145.44 versus bar 117 range 208.31), and no bear trend bar has follow-through."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars; window low 1368.42 (bar 10, open_time 1780704000000) and window high 2850 (bar 117, open_time 1789948800000); first close 2009.45 versus last close 2686.59.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to 1568.55, taking price to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 and leaves a 200.13-point lower tail (low 1368.42 versus close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-35 form a two-sided range with repeated highs at 1725.85 (bar 18) and 1845.09 (bar 19) and repeated lows at 1512.91 (bar 30) and 1551.60 (bar 34); bull and bear reversal bars alternate.", "Bars 36-49 rise on two wide bull trend bars (bar 36: 1608.68 to 1701.02; bar 48: 1775.60 to 1889.93, high 1891.66), reaching the 1944.39 high at bar 49.", "Bars 50-83 form a long, tight range: high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51); bars 73-83 overlap inside 1863.68-1937.76.", "Bar 84 (open_time 1787097600000) is a large bull trend bar, 1916.51 to 2252.16, closing 96% of its 377.29 range, the widest bar in the window, above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bars 87-113 hold a broad range: low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike highs at 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 break upward: bar 114 closes 2612.02 (85% of its 206.65 range), bar 115 taps 2700, bar 117 reaches a new window high 2850 and closes 2775.61 with a 74.39-point upper tail.", "Bars 118-120 pull back: bar 119 is a bear bar closing 2684.16 in the lower quarter of its 145.44 range; bar 120 is a small bull bar (open 2684.16, close 2686.59) with low 2633.31, holding above the 2680 range top.", "Higher swing lows: 1368.42 (bar 10), 1512.91 (bar 30), 1597.72 (bar 36), 1803.74 (bar 51), 2357.18 (bar 98), 2633.31 (bar 120). Higher swing highs: 1944.39 (bar 49), 2771 (bar 86), 2850 (bar 117)."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Sell climax ending the window's down leg: bars 6-10 post five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail.", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2006.17"}, {"description": "Post-sell-off two-sided range (bars 11-35): repeated tests of the 1512.91-1551.60 low area and the 1725.85-1845.09 high area, with most closes between 1550 and 1730.", "end_time_ms": 1782950399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Long, tight range (bars 50-83): high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51), compressing into 1863.68-1937.76 for bars 73-83 immediately before the bar 84 breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull breakout and spike (bars 84-86): bar 84 runs 1916.51 to 2252.16 and closes near its high, above the 1974.46 range top; follow-through carries to the spike high 2771 at bar 86.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Broad post-spike range (bars 87-113): low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike attempts at 2557.46, 2680 and 2609.02 all closed back inside.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Current bull leg (bars 114-117): two strong bull trend bars plus an overlapping pair break above the 2680 range top and the 2771 swing high to a new window high 2850; bars 118-120 pull back to 2633.31, still above 2680.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2850, or a bar closing in the upper third of its range above 2775.61, would confirm the breakout-spike read and favor trend continuation.", "Two consecutive closes below 2633.31 (bar 120 low) would indicate a failed breakout and rotation back into the 2357.18-2680 range, moving phase toward range.", "A strong bear trend bar closing below 2357.18 (bar 98 low) would end the sequence of higher swing lows and shift the regime read to trading-range or transition-unclear.", "Continued overlapping bars and closes inside 2633.31-2786.81 without reaching 2850 again would raise the odds that the last leg is a channel within a broad top, changing phase to channel and lowering always-in relevance.", "A pullback that holds above the 2436.87-2514.13 breakout area and then produces a close above 2786.81 would keep the bull-trend read while confirming the pullback as a buy-the-close-style continuation leg of the channel."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Every bull extreme in the window is rejected by a large upper tail: 124.48 at 2680 (1789128000000), 94.95 at 2609.02 (1789416000000), 126.85 at 2850 (1789977600000); those highs were never revisited, which reads as buy-climax/range behavior rather than accepted breakout.", "Since 1789992000000 price has not exceeded 2804.59 and traded back below the entire 1789977600000 bar range (low 2658.06) to 2633.31, leaving a lower high 2804.59 versus 2850 - the strongest mtr-like argument against a clean bull-trend read.", "Late responsive selling is visible: bar opening 1790164800000 opens 2726.71 and closes 2659 (near its low 2648.49), and the last close 2686.59 is below the 2633.31-2804.59 midpoint, so the recent 20 bars are two-sided, not one-sided.", "First-half structure was a 39-bar range (2411.04-2528.8), and the prior breakout highs 2680 and 2609.02 both failed, showing that strong legs in this window have not converted into sustained trend outside a channel-with-pullbacks pattern."], "evidence_for": ["Window is net higher (open 2454.35 to close 2686.59) and the window's highest high 2850 (bar opening 1789977600000) occurs late rather than early.", "After the window low 2358.62 the sequence of swing lows rises (2435.71, 2569.8, 2633.31) and the last three bars extend that with higher lows 2640/2660.49/2676.02.", "Bull spike bars close near their highs and are followed by holding bars: 1789732800000 closes 2578.6, 1789747200000 closes 2636.28, and 1789977600000 opens 2658.81 and closes 2723.15 with bars 1789992000000-1790020800000 holding 2718.09-2804.59.", "The pullback from 2804.59 stopped at 2633.31, above the 2569.8 pullback low, so the up sequence did not print a lower low before the recovery to 2694.09."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars, 1788566400000 to 1790280000000; first bar opens 2454.35, last bar closes 2686.59 (+9.5% net over the window).", "First ~39 bars rotate inside 2411.04 (low of the bar opening 1789041600000) to 2528.8 (high of the bar opening 1788739200000) with neither edge accepted.", "Bar opening 1789128000000 (open 2457.12) spiked to 2680 and closed 2555.52, a 124.48 upper tail; that high was not exceeded for roughly the next 40 bars.", "Bar opening 1789416000000 printed high 2609.02 and closed 2514.07 (94.95 upper tail), then the bar opening 1789473600000 ranged 93.62 and closed 2423.29, carrying price to the window low 2358.62 (bar opening 1789488000000).", "From 2358.62 swing lows rise: 2435.71, 2569.8 (bar opening 1789862400000), 2633.31; bull spike bars appear at 1789732800000 (close 2578.6) and 1789747200000 (close 2636.28).", "Bar opening 1789977600000 opened 2658.81, spiked to 2850 (window high) and closed 2723.15, a 126.85 upper tail; the next three bars held 2718.09-2804.59.", "Since that spike price stayed between 2633.31 (low of the bar opening 1790236800000) and 2804.59 (high of the bar opening 1790020800000); last close 2686.59 sits below that range's midpoint.", "Final three bars have ranges 54.37, 38.9 and 19.76 with higher lows 2640, 2660.49, 2676.02 and highs capped at 2694.37-2699.39 (two-sided contraction)."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening trading range: 39 bars rotating between repeated tests of 2528.8-2511.12 on top and 2441.33-2411.04 below, with no sustained follow-through either way.", "end_time_ms": 1789113600000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788566400000, "upper_boundary": "2528.8"}, {"description": "Bull spike bar (open 2457.12, high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52) that broke above the opening range and left a 124.48 upper tail; price faded back toward 2444.19 instead of following through.", "end_time_ms": 1789128000000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2444.19", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Bear leg from the 2609.02 high (bar opening 1789416000000, 94.95 upper tail) down to the window low 2358.62, including a 93.62-range bear bar closing 2423.29.", "end_time_ms": 1789488000000, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789416000000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Bull leg from 2358.62 to the 2850 spike high: push to 2658.79 (1789977600000 area), pullback to 2569.8, then a two-bar spike; rising swing lows throughout, with pullbacks overlapping prior bars.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Range since the spike high: 2633.31 to 2804.59 with overlapping bars and the 2850 extreme unrecovered; current close 2686.59 is mid-range.", "end_time_ms": 1790280000000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Possible mtr-like topping attempt: spike high 2850 with a 126.85 upper tail, lower high 2804.59, then a break below the spike bar's low 2658.06 to 2633.31 - but bulls recovered above 2686 and the pattern is unconfirmed.", "end_time_ms": 1790280000000, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Final three bars: ranges 54.37/38.9/19.76 with higher lows 2640, 2660.49, 2676.02 and highs held to 2694.37-2699.39, i.e. two-sided contraction immediately below the range top.", "end_time_ms": 1790280000000, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2640", "start_time_ms": 1790251200000, "upper_boundary": "2699.39"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2804.59 with a following bar holding that level would confirm a bull breakout from the 2633.31-2804.59 range and return 2850 to the structure as the active extreme.", "A close below 2633.31 followed by acceptance below 2569.8 would break the higher-low sequence and shift the read toward a bear leg or a broader trading range with 2804.59-2850 as a lower-high resistance area.", "Continued sub-25-point